    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## ISO-VG Viscosity Grade Standards\n\nISO VG stands for \"International Standards Organization Viscosity Grade\" and uses a numbering system ranging from 2 to 1500.\n\n### Temperature Conversion Formulas\n- **Celsius to Fahrenheit:** tF = 9/5 × tC + 32\n- **Fahrenheit to Celsius:** tC = 5/9 × (tF - 32)\n\n### Viscosity Unit Conversion Formulas\n- **1 reyns (lb·s/in²) = 6896.55 Pa·s**\n- **1 cSt (centiStoke) = 1 cP (centiPoise) / SG**\n- **Where SG = specific gravity of oil**\n\n### Common ISO-VG Applications\n- **ISO-VG 22, 32:** Light hydraulic oils, precision machinery\n- **ISO-VG 46:** Standard hydraulic and turbine oils\n- **ISO-VG 68, 100:** Heavy hydraulic applications\n- **ISO-VG 150, 220:** Gear oils, circulating oils\n- **ISO-VG 320+:** Heavy industrial gear oils"
